---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getSettings } from '../../lib/settings';
import { href } from '../../lib/url';

const settings = await getSettings();
---

<Base
  title="Help with the archive"
  description="How to contribute to, correct, or request removal from the Bala Regatta archive."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap stack">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <a href={href('/archives')}>Archives</a> &middot; Corrections
      </p>
      <h1>Help with the archive</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The archive is assembled from programmes, results sheets, newspaper clippings and
        memory. It will contain mistakes, and it is missing far more than it holds.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If a name is misspelled, a year is wrong, or a race is credited to the wrong crew, please
        tell us. Where possible, say what your correction is based on — a programme, a photograph,
        a clipping — so the record can cite it.
      </p>

      <h2>Material we would love to see</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Official programmes, of any year.</li>
        <li>Results sheets and prize lists, however scrappy.</li>
        <li>Photographs, especially ones where you can name the people in them.</li>
        <li>Newspaper clippings.</li>
        <li>Committee records, minutes, or lists of past commodores and officers.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Originals do not need to leave your hands — a phone photograph of each page is enough to
        work from.
      </p>

      <h2>Names of living people</h2>
      <p>
        This archive names people who are still alive, because a regatta record without names is
        not a record. We try to handle that carefully:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Names appear as the original source printed them, which is often just initials and a
          surname.
        </li>
        <li>
          A person only gets a page of their own where records can be reasonably connected to one
          individual.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not publish addresses, birthdates, or contact details, and we do not name children
          beyond what a published programme already did.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>If you would rather not appear, just ask.</strong> We will remove your page and can
        reduce your name to initials in the results, or take it out entirely. No explanation
        needed.
      </p>

      <h2>Photographs</h2>
      <p>
        If you hold the rights to a photograph on this site and would like it credited differently
        or taken down, please get in touch and we will act on it.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      {
        settings.email ? (
          <p>
            <a class="button" href={`mailto:${settings.email}?subject=Bala%20Regatta%20archive`}>
              Email the archive
            </a>
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>The contact address is in the footer of every page.</p>
        )
      }

      <aside class="todo">
        <p>
          <strong>For the committee to agree before launch.</strong> The commitments on this page —
          particularly around removing names of living people and handling photograph rights — are
          a sensible default, not a decision anyone has ratified. Please read them and change them
          to match what the association is actually willing to do, because publishing a promise you
          will not keep is worse than publishing none.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
